what rye_struct_fields reads RED fleet-wide on a Mantra structure: Line declares text gen pos site run ord and its placard says text gen pos site run. Diff is stale behind it -- declares site inserts deletes replaces after against a placard of site inserts deletes. Both are the anchor and order-key work landing and the records staying behind, which is also true of weave.rye's own head: it still promises every insert lands at the END and calls the anchor a seam rather than a lap, while apply reads diff.after at line 1413. Move the two placards forward with dated reasons, repair the head and annotate's header to the residue that is actually true, book the row.
